WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:02.801
-She's Oscar-nominated
for her movie

00:00:02.801 --> 00:00:05.300
"Promising Young Woman,"
and she's hosting

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.300
"Saturday Night Live"
this weekend

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:08.767
with musical guest Kid Cudi.

00:00:08.767 --> 00:00:11.667
Please welcome Carey Mulligan!

00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:13.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.968 --> 00:00:16.467
♪♪

00:00:16.467 --> 00:00:18.534
Come on!
That's what I'm talking about!

00:00:18.534 --> 00:00:19.767
Great to see you.
-Hi.

00:00:19.767 --> 00:00:21.200
-Not too sha--
Oh, my. Standing O!

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.734
Come on. Welcome.
Please have a seat.

00:00:22.734 --> 00:00:24.734
-Oh, come on.
-Carey, thank you so much

00:00:24.734 --> 00:00:26.367
for being here.
-Thank you.

00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:29.968
-Now we're going to face off
in a game called "Box of Lies."

00:00:29.968 --> 00:00:31.267
-[ Exhales slowly ]

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:32.968
-♪ Box of Lies, box of Lies ♪

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:35.734
♪ Box of Lies, box of Lies ♪

00:00:35.734 --> 00:00:37.834
♪ Box of Lies ♪

00:00:37.834 --> 00:00:39.434
-Now, here's how it works.

00:00:39.434 --> 00:00:42.167
We have nine mystery boxes
containing objects

00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:43.901
no one has ever seen before.

00:00:43.901 --> 00:00:46.968
Okay, on your turn, you pick
a box, take out the object,

00:00:46.968 --> 00:00:48.834
and describe it
to your opponent.

00:00:48.834 --> 00:00:50.934
Then they have to guess
if you're lying

00:00:50.934 --> 00:00:52.200
or telling the truth.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:53.534
We're going to play
three rounds.

00:00:53.534 --> 00:00:55.200
I don't want to look at you
because I think

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.534
maybe you're already
playing the game.

00:00:57.534 --> 00:00:59.300
Carey, you pick the first box.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:00.868
-I go first? Okay.
-Yeah.

00:01:00.868 --> 00:01:02.267
-This one!
-Yeah.

00:01:02.267 --> 00:01:04.000
-Ooh, it's heavy! Okay.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.934
All right. Oof.

00:01:05.934 --> 00:01:08.400
-Okay. It did feel --
It did sound heavy.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.067
So that's the first clue.
-Oh, no.

00:01:10.067 --> 00:01:14.300
-Yep. Okay.
I think I got this one.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:15.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:18.367
Carey, when you're ready.

00:01:18.367 --> 00:01:21.200
You can tell me.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.067
What is in your box?

00:01:23.067 --> 00:01:25.834
-It's another box.

00:01:25.834 --> 00:01:30.701
And it's got sort of
pink spaghetti

00:01:30.701 --> 00:01:33.234
with glitter

00:01:33.234 --> 00:01:37.901
and, like, tiny little trolls
all around in a circle

00:01:37.901 --> 00:01:41.167
like they're at
some sort of meeting.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:44.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.901 --> 00:01:47.868
-So in your box is another box.

00:01:47.868 --> 00:01:49.234
-Yeah.

00:01:49.234 --> 00:01:50.701
-Okay. And in that box...
-Yeah.

00:01:50.701 --> 00:01:52.400
-...there's a spaghetti
in the middle

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.934
and then trolls standing
around it like it's a ritual.

00:01:54.934 --> 00:01:57.934
-Like a ritual thing.
-A ritual, yeah.

00:01:57.934 --> 00:01:59.501
-Yeah.

00:01:59.501 --> 00:02:02.000
-And they're --
The dolls are touching hands?

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:03.734
-They're not touching hands.

00:02:03.734 --> 00:02:05.567
They're socially distanced,
but they're --

00:02:05.567 --> 00:02:07.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.501 --> 00:02:09.067
-They're
socially distant trolls.

00:02:09.067 --> 00:02:11.100
-They're --
It's sort of like they're at --

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:13.100
Yeah, they're at a big meeting.

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:15.000
And there's, like,
little baby ones, big ones,

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.067
and all their hair is like this.

00:02:18.067 --> 00:02:19.868
-Classic trolls. Yeah.
-Classic troll. Yeah.

00:02:19.868 --> 00:02:22.100
-That would be weird. Why would
you have to describe their hair?

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:23.167
That's interesting, right?

00:02:23.167 --> 00:02:24.701
-I don't know
why I would have to.

00:02:24.701 --> 00:02:27.000
-Yeah. Because maybe
it's not real maybe.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:28.133
-Aw.
-Aw. Too bad.

00:02:28.133 --> 00:02:30.367
Maybe you're just making
this whole thing up.

00:02:30.367 --> 00:02:33.601
Trolls, spaghetti.
Another box in the box.

00:02:33.601 --> 00:02:37.100
You described that
they have hair, crazy hair.

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:39.334
Yeah. Oh, really?
Trolls have crazy hair?

00:02:39.334 --> 00:02:42.133
Wow. Thanks for the description.
I didn't know what that meant.

00:02:42.133 --> 00:02:44.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.934 --> 00:02:46.968
Or are you just
being so obvious...

00:02:46.968 --> 00:02:48.601
-So specific.

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:50.067
-...that I'm spinning myself up?

00:02:50.067 --> 00:02:51.100
-Yeah.
-You know?

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.968
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:53.968 --> 00:02:56.701
-[ Chuckles ]
Carey Mulligan.

00:02:56.701 --> 00:02:58.734
-Yeah.

00:02:58.734 --> 00:03:00.834
-You tell the truth.

00:03:00.834 --> 00:03:02.067
-I lied!

00:03:02.067 --> 00:03:03.667
-Oh, my gosh!

00:03:03.667 --> 00:03:05.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:05.367 --> 00:03:07.534
[ Laughs ] Unbelievable!

00:03:07.534 --> 00:03:08.667
What is it? Let me see it.

00:03:08.667 --> 00:03:10.901
-Look. It's a hat
full of bolognese.

00:03:10.901 --> 00:03:12.434
-How did you do that?
You are unb--

00:03:12.434 --> 00:03:14.367
Of course, you were
going to be great at this.

00:03:14.367 --> 00:03:17.000
Are you kidding me?
You are a fantastic actor.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.634
Oh, my gosh. I honestly --

00:03:19.634 --> 00:03:21.868
You are so good!
-Thank you!

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:23.501
-All right. Now it is
my turn to pick a box.

00:03:23.501 --> 00:03:25.300
Which number, everyone?

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:28.334
[ Audience shouting numbers ]

00:03:28.334 --> 00:03:29.934
It's either three or five.

00:03:29.934 --> 00:03:32.367
[ Audience shouting numbers ]

00:03:32.367 --> 00:03:34.067
Now you're just --
Now you're just grunting.

00:03:34.067 --> 00:03:35.834
[ Imitates shouting ]

00:03:35.834 --> 00:03:38.033
Yeah. "Ehh" is nothing.

00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:39.534
Ehh? Four?

00:03:39.534 --> 00:03:41.367
[ Audience shouting numbers ]

00:03:42.901 --> 00:03:44.400
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:45.868
[ Exhales heavily ]

00:03:45.868 --> 00:03:49.534
[ Grunting ]

00:03:49.534 --> 00:03:51.033
[ Thud ]

00:03:51.033 --> 00:03:53.000
-All right.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:55.100
-Wow. That was heavy.
-Yeah.

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:57.100
-[ Exhales shakily ]
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:59.834
♪♪

00:03:59.834 --> 00:04:01.400
-All right.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:03.400
[British accent] All right.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:07.167
Hello! Hello!

00:04:07.167 --> 00:04:10.634
♪♪

00:04:10.634 --> 00:04:13.033
-What's in the box?

00:04:13.033 --> 00:04:14.634
-[ Chuckles ]

00:04:14.634 --> 00:04:18.200
♪♪

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:20.634
There's a connection to you.

00:04:20.634 --> 00:04:23.200
-Okay.
-It's a classic.

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:26.400
It's a tiny tennis racket
holding a classic novel,

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:27.667
"The Great Gatsby."

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:29.501
-A tennis racket
is holding a novel?

00:04:29.501 --> 00:04:32.868
-It's a tiny -- It's more
of a stand, a book stand.

00:04:32.868 --> 00:04:36.801
Holding a novel.
The novel is "The Great Gatsby."

00:04:36.801 --> 00:04:39.734
But it's "The Great Tatsby."

00:04:39.734 --> 00:04:42.634
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.634 --> 00:04:45.367
And it's Leo
giving you a tattoo.

00:04:45.367 --> 00:04:47.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.534 --> 00:04:49.300
♪♪

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:51.367
-Uh-huh.
I don't understand why you said

00:04:51.367 --> 00:04:53.634
it was a tennis racket.
What is it that? I don't --

00:04:53.634 --> 00:04:56.033
-A tennis racket
is holding the book up.

00:04:56.033 --> 00:04:58.234
-A tenn-- Does
the tennis racket have arms?

00:04:58.234 --> 00:04:59.968
Like, is it a cartoon?

00:04:59.968 --> 00:05:02.234
-It's a tiny tennis --
It's a book holder.

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:03.934
It's like a --
-I've never seen

00:05:03.934 --> 00:05:06.734
a book-holding tennis racket.

00:05:06.734 --> 00:05:08.133
-It's a novelty.

00:05:08.133 --> 00:05:09.901
It's a tennis racket
on its side,

00:05:09.901 --> 00:05:11.834
and the book
is in the middle of the racket.

00:05:11.834 --> 00:05:13.300
-Okay.
-Like a bookshelf thing.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:15.267
Like, have you ever seen
two hands on the end

00:05:15.267 --> 00:05:16.601
of a book shelf?

00:05:16.601 --> 00:05:18.033
Like it's novelty.

00:05:18.033 --> 00:05:20.701
-Yeah, but that's not -- Okay.
Is this an American thing?

00:05:20.701 --> 00:05:22.701
-[ Laughs ] Sure.
-Okay.

00:05:22.701 --> 00:05:23.968
-Sure it is.

00:05:23.968 --> 00:05:25.901
It's an old-timey
wooden tennis racket.

00:05:25.901 --> 00:05:27.033
-And it's holding a book?

00:05:27.033 --> 00:05:29.033
So, what --
Is the book a picture of us?

00:05:29.033 --> 00:05:32.267
-It's a picture of you.
Leo is giving you a tattoo.

00:05:32.267 --> 00:05:34.567
"The Great Tatsby"
is what it says.

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:36.267
-"The Great Tatsby." Okay.
-Yeah.

00:05:36.267 --> 00:05:38.634
-Any other details
you want to -- Nothing else?

00:05:38.634 --> 00:05:41.901
-You're getting a barbed wire --

00:05:41.901 --> 00:05:44.067
Barbed-wire tattoo on your arm.

00:05:44.067 --> 00:05:45.834
-That's what the tattoo is of?
-That's correct.

00:05:45.834 --> 00:05:47.434
-Okay.
-And you're not enjoying it.

00:05:47.434 --> 00:05:50.067
-Can I tell you what I think?
-Yeah, I would love to hear it.

00:05:50.067 --> 00:05:53.534
I can't wait.

00:05:53.534 --> 00:05:55.334
-I think you're lying.

00:05:55.334 --> 00:05:56.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:56.634 --> 00:05:59.334
[ Ding! ]

00:05:59.334 --> 00:06:01.734
Oh, wow!

00:06:01.734 --> 00:06:04.167
-Chess pizza.
-That's great.

00:06:04.167 --> 00:06:06.467
-Was it the aroma of pizza?

00:06:06.467 --> 00:06:08.534
-Is it an actual pizza?
-Yes.

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:09.834
-Oh, wow. It is.

00:06:09.834 --> 00:06:12.200
That's not far off
my troll ritual.

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:14.434
-Oh. Actually --
Weirdly. you're right.

00:06:14.434 --> 00:06:16.033
Wow. It's like you ca--

00:06:16.033 --> 00:06:20.100
This is the trickiest game
of "Box of Lies" we ever played.

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:22.701
You're actually
creating the truth.

00:06:22.701 --> 00:06:24.167
No one's ever done that.
-No? Okay.

00:06:24.167 --> 00:06:26.167
-Gosh. You're a mastermind.
All right. Here we go.

00:06:26.167 --> 00:06:27.968
So it's a close game.
But you know what?

00:06:27.968 --> 00:06:29.801
This last round
is worth 10,000 points.

00:06:29.801 --> 00:06:31.734
-Oh, my gosh.
-So whoever wins this round

00:06:31.734 --> 00:06:33.701
is the champion.

00:06:33.701 --> 00:06:37.100
Now, Carey, you're up.
Please choose a box.

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:38.567
-Okay.

00:06:38.567 --> 00:06:40.934
[ Audience shouting numbers ]

00:06:40.934 --> 00:06:42.234
-[ Jimmy grunting ]

00:06:42.234 --> 00:06:44.234
[ Laughs ]

00:06:44.234 --> 00:06:45.767
-Unnnnnhh!

00:06:45.767 --> 00:06:48.667
-Nice acting job. Oh, my gosh.
So I already know it's light.

00:06:48.667 --> 00:06:49.968
-All right.
-Yep.

00:06:49.968 --> 00:06:52.033
-No problem, no problem.

00:06:52.033 --> 00:06:56.601
Number two. The deuce!
That's what they call it.

00:06:56.601 --> 00:06:59.834
♪♪

00:06:59.834 --> 00:07:01.701
Okay, and the wheels
are spinning.

00:07:01.701 --> 00:07:03.767
I can already see.

00:07:03.767 --> 00:07:05.734
She's choosing.
She's choosing.

00:07:05.734 --> 00:07:09.300
-This is actually "SNL"-themed.
-Oh, really?

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:10.434
-Yeah.

00:07:10.434 --> 00:07:12.100
-Yeah. A lot of themes
going tonight.

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:16.300
-It's -- Well, it's a themed --
It's a themed thing.

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:19.601
It's a mug, a T-shirt,

00:07:19.601 --> 00:07:22.934
and, like, a beach towel
of some description.

00:07:22.934 --> 00:07:25.100
From Tracy Morgan?

00:07:26.968 --> 00:07:29.467
So it's like a --
-What you just pulled out

00:07:29.467 --> 00:07:32.267
of that box was a mug,
a T-shirt, and beach towel?

00:07:32.267 --> 00:07:35.234
-Yeah, but, like, wrapped up.
Wrapped up.

00:07:35.234 --> 00:07:37.133
-How wrapped
is that beach towel?

00:07:37.133 --> 00:07:39.634
Is this, like, an American --
a British thing?

00:07:39.634 --> 00:07:42.367
-No, it has like --
-Like a tiny beach towel?

00:07:42.367 --> 00:07:44.501
-Yeah, it's like for a baby.

00:07:44.501 --> 00:07:47.067
-[ Laughs ] That's
a good business, by the way.

00:07:47.067 --> 00:07:48.734
Baby beach towel.
-Baby beach towels.

00:07:48.734 --> 00:07:50.267
-So you're saying it is a mug.

00:07:50.267 --> 00:07:52.400
-It's a mug, it's a beach towel,
and it's a --

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:53.734
-[ Laughs ]
-[ Laughs ]

00:07:53.734 --> 00:07:55.767
-Oh, no. Oh, no!

00:07:55.767 --> 00:07:59.100
It's sinking fast!
It's sinking fast!

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:01.734
-Or am I just brilliant?
-No.

00:08:01.734 --> 00:08:04.701
That already happened
the first round.

00:08:04.701 --> 00:08:06.200
You were brilliant
in the first round.

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:07.901
-Yeah.
-This one, I think this one --

00:08:07.901 --> 00:08:09.167
You came in with this one.

00:08:09.167 --> 00:08:10.601
-Yeah.
-This is your safety lie.

00:08:10.601 --> 00:08:11.868
-Yeah.
-And what happened was,

00:08:11.868 --> 00:08:13.300
you kind of freaked out
and you go,

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:15.334
"Am I going to tell the truth
and just say what it is?

00:08:15.334 --> 00:08:16.801
That would really get
Jimmy going.

00:08:16.801 --> 00:08:18.634
Or do I make up a whole lie?"

00:08:18.634 --> 00:08:21.367
Your pre-made lie
that you probably talked

00:08:21.367 --> 00:08:22.667
to your publicist about before.

00:08:22.667 --> 00:08:25.133
You go, "Saturday Night Live,"
Tracy Morgan.

00:08:25.133 --> 00:08:27.000
That will make Jimmy guess that.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:29.100
And you think I'm that easy

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:31.300
to put the lock in
and flip the switch

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:34.767
and open my -- err -- door,
hop into the brain, and go...

00:08:34.767 --> 00:08:37.200
[British accent]
..."Good day, love!"

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:41.033
[Normal voice] Try again.
You picked the wrong day.

00:08:41.033 --> 00:08:44.133
What I'm trying to say
is, Carey Mulligan...

00:08:44.133 --> 00:08:45.334
you lie!

00:08:45.334 --> 00:08:47.000
-Unh!
-Yes!

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:49.734
♪♪

00:08:49.734 --> 00:08:52.367
[ Laughs ] That's not bad!

00:08:52.367 --> 00:08:54.801
[ Laughs ]
That actually is not bad.

00:08:54.801 --> 00:08:56.300
You know how I kind of knew?
-Yeah.

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:58.501
-'Cause you kind of smiled
a little bit when you saw it.

00:08:58.501 --> 00:09:00.968
-I know, I know.
But I tried so hard not to.

00:09:00.968 --> 00:09:03.467
-I know.
But your dimples gave you away!

00:09:03.467 --> 00:09:06.434
There is Carey Mulligan,
everybody!

00:09:06.434 --> 00:09:07.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:07.767 --> 00:09:09.968
Clearly better at this
than I am.

